<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<index; (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null) => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)));</code>

This assert statement ensures that for every valid index `i` less than the specified `index`, the element at position `i` in the list after the operation is either `null` if it was `null` before the operation, or remains unchanged if it was not `null`.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));</code>
--------------------
